index 184ea54..fdab2bc 100644
--- a/docs/007-architecture.md
+++ b/docs/007-architecture.md
@@ -194,6 +194,22 @@ Plugins receive `SourceHost`: the registry and `context(kind)`. The kind itself
 
 That context supplies deployment and commands, setup readiness (`ready`, `configured`, `problem`), configuration, `receive`, `atomic`, and typed `state`. It also exposes Thread reads and metadata writes, Ticket reads and binding/closure commands, Trigger reads, `notify` through Outbox, and `report` for declared health entries.
 
+### Scoped execution controls
+
+`SourceContext.execution.version === 1` is the capability probe. All three methods take `threadKey` and `ticketId`; controls also require `expectedAssignmentId` and `expectedControlSeq` (initially 0). The adapter checks the registered Source kind against the stored Thread and origin Trigger, the origin Thread membership, and the Ticket subscription (never a context-only subscription). Sources remain responsible for caller authentication and conversation ownership. No method accepts a Session id or the main Session.
+
+- `read({threadKey,ticketId,cursor?,limit?})` uses alpha cold Controller `inspect` plus one `page`, or RC `events`/`page` with its exact returned cursor, never `follow` or `resolveAgent`. `limit: 0` reads only execution state and performs no Session I/O. The cursor pins `throughSeq` and optionally `beforeSeq`; records keep the actual worker seq/time. Each response is capped at 100 visible records and 128 KiB. It projects text and lifecycle facts, not reasoning, system prompts, credentials or raw tool input/output. `history`, `truncated`, `hasMore` and `nextCursor` distinguish filtered, unavailable and incomplete history. Alpha's initial `inspect` materializes the persisted prefix internally; page/output work is bounded, not that SDK's initial internal read.
+- `interrupt({threadKey,ticketId,expectedAssignmentId,expectedControlSeq})` appends `interrupted` to `Ticket.executionEvents` in the same transaction as the durable cancellation effect. Only after commit does DshExecutor cancel the worker and stop its background work, keeping its inbox. An exact replay of the last operation is idempotent; a stale Stop after continuation conflicts even though the Assignment is reused. Neither Ticket nor Assignment ends, and its Mandate and subscriptions remain.
+- `resume({threadKey,ticketId,expectedAssignmentId,expectedControlSeq})` appends `continued`, revalidates the Mandate and queues an internal continuation or the pending launch on the same Assignment. It does not retry or recreate the workspace/branch. It refuses continuation until interruption is verified settled. Text is not accepted: human instructions must enter through `Source.receive` as audited Triggers.
+
+`SourceExecutionError` exposes only fixed `name`, `status`, `code` and `message`: invalid input 400, scope refusal 403, missing execution 404, state/CAS conflict 409, operational failure 503. No internal stack/cause/path/provider detail crosses the interface.
+
+`state` describes the Assignment lifecycle; `activity` reads the existing SDK registry/preparation map as `running`, `idle`, `cold`, `preparing` or `unknown`, never by activating an Agent.
+
+A paused execution is a durable user hold, not by itself proof of SDK cancellation. `interruption` reports `requested`, `settled` or `failed`. DshExecutor stores a separate cancellation receipt under `KV.executor.interruption`, matched to the control generation. `settled` requires the SDK worker to acknowledge idle, workspace preparation to exit, no running jobs and no live subagents. Cancellation failures remain visible and the durable effect retries. The foreground interrupt waits at most one second; a longer stop remains `requested`, and callers poll state-only reads rather than claiming it stopped. An interrupted pending prepare command receives an abort signal; continuation never invents a new directory or branch.
+
+`pausedExecution` derives the hold from the last journal event for the current Assignment. Launches, deliveries, restart recovery, delayed retries, idle callbacks, worker tools and reports recheck that durable hold; asynchronous callbacks additionally compare the control journal generation. A late report cannot clear a pause or complete the Ticket. Existing management `stopTicket` (terminal) and `retryTicket` (new Assignment) keep their meanings; retry refuses an interrupted execution until explicitly continued.
+
 ### DshExecutor
 
 `DshExecutor` (`src/executor/dsh.ts`) provides one Session and directory per Ticket. `start` and `deliver` enqueue `launch` and `delivery` effects. `stop` cancels the turn through `Store.afterCommit`, so a rolled-back end does not stop the worker.
